-names>M</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Carranza</surname> <given-names>C</given-names></string-name>, <etal/><article-title>Emergence of <italic>Neisseria meningitidis</italic> with decreased susceptibility to ciprofloxacin in Argentina.</article-title><source>J Antimicrob Chemother</source> <year>2005</year>;<volume>55</volume>:<fpage>596</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>7</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/jac/dki048</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15728148</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R5"><label>5. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Chu</surname> <given-names>YW</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Cheung</surname> <given-names>TK</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Tung</surname> <given-names>V</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Tiu</surname> <given-names>F</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Lo</surname> <given-names>J</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Lam</surname> <given-names>R</given-names></string-name>, <etal/><article-title>A blood isolate of <italic>Neisseria meningitidis</italic> showing reduced susceptibility to quinolones in Hong Kong.</article-title><source>Int J Antimicrob Agents</source> <year>2007</year>;<volume>30</volume>:<fpage>94</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>5</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.ijantimicag.2006.11.028</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17408928</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R6"><label>6. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Singhal</surname> <given-names>S</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Purnapatre</surname> <given-names>KP</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Kalia</surname> <given-names>V</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Dube</surname> <given-names>S</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Nair</surname> <given-names>D</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Deb</surname> <given-names>M</g